<header><p class="st-kicker">other · Scandinavia and the Baltic</p><h1 class="st-title">Governorate of Estonia</h1><p class="st-meta">1721 CE – 1917 CE · capital Reval</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">Russian imperial province of northern Estonia, governed for nearly two centuries by Baltic German nobles and the setting of the Estonian national awakening.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>After <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peter-the-great">Peter the Great</a> conquered the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/swedish-estonia">Swedish Duchy of Estonia</a> (1561-1721) in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/great-northern-war">Great Northern War</a>, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/treaty-of-nystad">Treaty of Nystad</a> in 1721 made it a province of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/russian-empire">Russian Empire</a>, with <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/reval">Reval</a> as its capital. Peter confirmed the privileges of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/baltic-germans">Baltic German</a> nobility, their Lutheran church and German as the language of administration.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>Under this Baltic special order, the Estonian knighthood ran local government, courts and the land, while Estonian peasants were serfs. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/serfdom">Serfdom</a> was abolished in 1816, though land remained with the nobles. In the late 19th century an Estonian national movement grew, and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russification">Russification</a> policies of the 1880s replaced German with Russian in schools and courts. <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/reval">Reval</a> became an industrial port and naval base.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>After the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/february-revolution">February Revolution</a> of 1917 the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/russian-republic">Russian Provisional Government</a> merged the governorate with the Estonian-speaking north of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/governorate-of-livonia">Governorate of Livonia</a> to form the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/autonomous-governorate-of-estonia">Autonomous Governorate of Estonia</a>, the forerunner of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/republic-of-estonia">Republic of Estonia</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/governorate-of-estonia.jpg" alt="Governorate of Estonia" width="320" height="189"><figcaption>Image: Milenioscuro · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Estonia_in_Russian_Empire_(1914).svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1721 CE – 1917 CE</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>other</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Reval</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Lutheran Christianity</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Estonian, German, Russian</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/estonia">Estonia</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Estland Governorate, Reval Governorate, Estonia Governorate</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1819&amp;focus=governorate-of-estonia" aria-label="Governorate of Estonia on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5201 181 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Governorate of Estonia lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5521 437L6487 457M5521 437L5521 437"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M6487 457h0M5521 437h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5521 437h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5521 437h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks its recorded location. <a href="/atlas?year=1819&amp;focus=governorate-of-estonia">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
